WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.041
name is Huckleberry Finn.

2
00:00:16.241 --> 00:00:20.963
If you've read a book called The Adventures of Tom Sawyer, you already know about me.

3
00:00:21.944 --> 00:00:23.764
But if you haven't, it doesn't matter.

4
00:00:24.725 --> 00:00:30.267
At the end of that book, my friend Tom and I found six thousand dollars, and each of

5
00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:31.888
us was allowed to keep half.

6
00:00:33.972 --> 00:00:40.958
Judge Thatcher invested the money for us, so Tom and I would never have to worry about not

7
00:00:41.058 --> 00:00:42.339
having enough money again.

8
00:00:45.842 --> 00:00:49.045
I didn't have a home, so the Widow Douglas took me in.

9
00:00:50.486 --> 00:00:52.608
She said she was going to civilize me.

10
00:00:53.789 --> 00:00:58.392
She made me wear new clean clothes, and sit at the table to eat my meals.

11
00:01:00.594 --> 00:01:05.790
But I missed the way I used to live, wearing my old rags and fixing my own supper.

12
00:01:06.831 --> 00:01:11.434
The widow had a sister, Miss Watson, who was determined to teach me to spell.

13
00:01:12.715 --> 00:01:14.276
I couldn't help wiggling around.

14
00:01:14.296 --> 00:01:17.678
"Huckleberry, sit up straight!"

15
00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:18.819
she scolded me.

16
00:01:18.839 --> 00:01:21.461
"Why can't you try to behave?"

17
00:01:22.581 --> 00:01:25.543
All I could think about was how I wanted to get away.

18
00:01:26.944 --> 00:01:33.321
I needed a change, but I knew the widow and her sister would never understand, so I didn't

19
00:01:33.401 --> 00:01:34.261
try to explain.

20
00:01:37.404 --> 00:01:41.527
By the time I went up to my room for bed, I felt sad and lonesome.

21
00:01:43.148 --> 00:01:46.251
I sat in a chair by the window and looked out at the night.

22
00:01:47.491 --> 00:01:50.113
I heard an owl hooting and a dog howling.

23
00:01:51.354 --> 00:01:55.037
It sounded to me as if they were mourning for someone who had died.

24
00:01:56.258 --> 00:01:58.480
It scared me, and I started to tremble.

25
00:02:00.572 --> 00:02:05.956
Then a spider crawled up on my shoulder, and when I shook it off, it fell into my

26
00:02:06.017 --> 00:02:07.278
candle and burned up.

27
00:02:09.079 --> 00:02:14.403
I knew that killing a spider could bring me very bad luck, so to keep the bad luck

28
00:02:14.463 --> 00:02:18.647
away, I turned myself around three times while crossing my chest.

29
00:02:19.748 --> 00:02:22.730
But I still felt afraid, and I trembled even harder.

30
00:02:25.612 --> 00:02:28.354
I sat there a long time until I calmed down.

31
00:02:29.675 --> 00:02:32.269
Finally, I heard the clock in the town of St.

32
00:02:32.329 --> 00:02:34.370
Petersburg strike 12 times.

33
00:02:36.891 --> 00:02:37.611
It was midnight.

34
00:02:38.972 --> 00:02:45.714
A twig snapped out in the darkness, and then I heard a little "Me-yow, me-yow," down in the

35
00:02:45.754 --> 00:02:49.876
yard. "Me-yow," I called back softly.

36
00:02:51.617 --> 00:02:55.978
Then I climbed out the window, onto the shed, and down to the ground.

37
00:02:56.819 --> 00:02:59.620
And sure enough, there was Tom waiting for me.

38
00:03:01.392 --> 00:03:03.854
Tom and I tiptoed through the widow's garden.

39
00:03:05.155 --> 00:03:07.856
As we passed the kitchen, I tripped over a root.

40
00:03:08.977 --> 00:03:14.241
Jim, Miss Watson's black slave, was sitting by the kitchen door when he heard the noise.

41
00:03:14.261 --> 00:03:16.302
"Who's that?"

42
00:03:16.762 --> 00:03:17.403
he called out.

43
00:03:18.303 --> 00:03:21.786
Then he came out into the garden and stood right between us.

44
00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:25.708
Tom and I stood completely still.

45
00:03:26.529 --> 00:03:28.290
Jim couldn't see us in the dark.

46
00:03:29.411 --> 00:03:32.105
"I know I heard something," Jim said.

47
00:03:32.125 --> 00:03:37.489
"I'm going to sit down here and listen until I hear that sound again."

48
00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:43.414
Well, first my ankle and my ear started to itch, and then my nose.

49
00:03:44.595 --> 00:03:49.679
I felt as if I'd die if I couldn't scratch, but if I did, Jim would know we

50
00:03:49.699 --> 00:03:50.139
were there.

51
00:03:52.461 --> 00:03:56.464
Just when I couldn't stand it any more, we heard Jim snoring.

52
00:03:57.245 --> 00:03:58.426
He had fallen asleep!

53
00:03:59.807 --> 00:04:02.634
Before we left, Tom played a trick on Jim.

54
00:04:03.855 --> 00:04:08.318
He crept over to Jim, took off his hat, and hung it on a branch.

55
00:04:09.199 --> 00:04:12.261
Tom said that Jim would think witches had moved his hat.

56
00:04:16.825 --> 00:04:22.790
Tom and I went into town where Ben Rogers, Joe Harper, and two or three other boys were

57
00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:23.511
waiting for us.

58
00:04:24.672 --> 00:04:29.576
We rowed a boat about four kilometers down the Mississippi River, and came ashore.

59
00:04:31.152 --> 00:04:35.594
There Tom led us to his secret cave, which had an entrance hidden by bushes.

60
00:04:38.815 --> 00:04:43.397
We lit our candles and crawled through a long passageway on our hands and knees.

61
00:04:46.318 --> 00:04:49.079
When we reached the cave, it was damp and cold.

62
00:04:49.099 --> 00:04:54.942
"We'll start a band of robbers called Tom Sawyer's Gang," Tom said.

63
00:04:54.962 --> 00:04:59.964
"Everyone who wants to join must take an oath and write his name in blood."

64
00:05:01.468 --> 00:05:02.288
Everyone agreed.

65
00:05:03.349 --> 00:05:06.230
Tom got out a piece of paper and wrote down the oath.

66
00:05:07.751 --> 00:05:12.593
It said that we had to promise to be loyal to the band and never tell its secrets.

67
00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:15.714
Anyone who told would be killed.

68
00:05:16.854 --> 00:05:22.116
We all said it was a very good oath, and Tom said that he got the words for

69
00:05:22.156 --> 00:05:24.237
it from books about pirates and robbers.

70
00:05:25.738 --> 00:05:30.720
Then Ben said that he thought the families of the boys who told secrets should be killed too.

71
00:05:32.092 --> 00:05:33.914
So Tom added that to the oath.

72
00:05:34.854 --> 00:05:37.216
Joe pointed out that I didn't have a family.

73
00:05:38.297 --> 00:05:43.761
Tom replied that I had a father, but the others objected that he'd disappeared a long time ago.

74
00:05:45.002 --> 00:05:48.425
Finally, I said I was willing to give them Miss Watson to kill.

75
00:05:52.609 --> 00:05:53.709
Everyone agreed to that.

76
00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:59.054
Then we all stuck our fingers with a pin, and made a mark on the paper with our

77
00:05:59.094 --> 00:06:04.049
blood. "Now," said Ben, "What is our gang going to do?"

78
00:06:04.069 --> 00:06:09.612
"We're going to wear masks and stop carriages on the road," Tom explained.

79
00:06:10.533 --> 00:06:13.375
"We'll kill the people and take their watches and money."

80
00:06:15.456 --> 00:06:20.899
It was getting very late, so we decided to meet again next week to decide which folks we

81
00:06:20.919 --> 00:06:21.779
would rob and kill.

82
00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:24.261
Then we all went home.

83
00:06:25.041 --> 00:06:29.184
By the time I climbed in my window at the widow's house it was almost dawn.

84
00:06:30.409 --> 00:06:33.999
My new clothes were covered with dirt and I was very tired.
